            "<p>Parallel Circuit</p>",
            "<p>Components connected in multiple paths</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hy2dm5i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5g3faop",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o1bwo32",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "jmw5ox2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iusdc1k",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8uxnu43",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oitro5b",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9yv2j05",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "avteuy4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8vrbubg",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7puz7kh",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ohm's Law (V = IR) applies strictly to ohmic conductors at constant physical parameters such as temperature.",
        "In a series circuit, electric current remains uniform while voltage divides; in a parallel circuit, voltage remains uniform while current divides.",
        "Frequently tested SI units: Current (Ampere), Resistance (Ohm), Power (Watt), and Magnetic Flux (Weber)."
      ],
      "id": "bid40fx"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sczuror",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "91vchez",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "soqg896",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "kh1ze7p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kbpkbio",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e9vgmf2",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qsmqosc",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ljrk0d3",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}